      "problem": "The DELETE /users/:id route omits the requireAdmin middleware. Both sibling routes in this router apply requireAdmin, and src/server.js adds no router-level guard.",
      "consequence": "Any caller who reaches the server can delete any user by id. This includes callers with no session.",
      "fix": "Add requireAdmin to the DELETE route, as the sibling routes do."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "file_path": "src/admin.js",
      "line_number": 22,
      "line_end": 25,
      "title": "Purge deletions float outside the handler",
      "description": "The purge handler passes an async callback to forEach, so nothing awaits or catches the db.removeUser promises. db.removeUser throws for an unknown id, and that rejection goes unhandled. One unknown id in a purge request raises an unhandled rejection, and Node then crashes the server. The response also reports every id as removed before any deletion finishes or fails. Await the deletions with Promise.allSettled before responding. Report the count of fulfilled deletions.",
      "suggested_change": "  const results = await Promise.allSettled(ids.map((id) => db.removeUser(id)));\n  res.json({ removed: results.filter((r) => r.status === \"fulfilled\").length });",
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The purge handler passes an async callback to forEach, so nothing awaits or catches the db.removeUser promises. db.removeUser throws for an unknown id, and that rejection goes unhandled.",
      "consequence": "One unknown id in a purge request raises an unhandled rejection, and Node then crashes the server. The response also reports every id as removed before any deletion finishes or fails.",
      "fix": "Await the deletions with Promise.allSettled before responding. Report the count of fulfilled deletions."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
